message: "If you use Fulcrum or the RVx Index, please cite this work."
title: "Fulcrum: Quantitative, Governed Granularity for Microservice Boundaries with the RVx Index"
authors:
  - family-names: Khan
    given-names: Viquar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3592-4162"
    email: vaquar.khan@gmail.com
type: software
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-21"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/vaquarkhan/fulcrum-rvx"
keywords:
  - microservices
  - service granularity
  - distributed monolith
  - software architecture
  - architecture fitness function
  - domain-driven design
  - software metrics
  - Conway's Law
abstract: >
  Fulcrum and the RVx Index provide a quantitative, governed fitness function for microservice
  boundary granularity. RVx fuses three signals, Kinetic Efficiency (runtime overhead from traces),
  Semantic Distinctness (evolutionary independence from version-control co-change), and Cognitive Load
  (complexity normalized against team capacity), into one bounded, diagnostic, per-boundary score
  whose weakest component names the remedy. The score is embedded in a sense-decide-actuate-verify
  governance loop that can run as a CI/CD fitness gate. The work contributes the metric, its proved
  structural properties, a measurement architecture, an adversarial and conformance treatment, a
  reproducible evaluation protocol, and a replicated real-AWS deployed-benchmark validation.
